  "portSplitNote": "Datasheet: \"Total number of RJ45 ports 8 (including eight combo ports)\", \"Total number of optical ports 28 (including eight combo ports)\", \"Number of 1GE combo ports 8\", \"Number of 1GE SFP ports 24 (including eight combo ports)\", \"Number of 10GE SFP+ ports 4\". The eight RJ45 ports are modelled as ge1..ge8 and the 1G cages as sfp1..sfp24, but the datasheet does not say WHICH eight cages are the combo ones, so no comboWith pairing is declared - the lab will not stop a second cable in a shared cage on this model.",
  "sourceUrl": "https://eo-sgp-cos.ruijie.com/Document/pdf/2025/12/9/RG-NBS3200-24SFP/8GT4XS_Datasheet_Official_2025-12-09.pdf",
  "notes": "Datasheet: \"Module slots No\", \"Reset button 1\", \"Maximum power consumption 41.8 W\", \"RAM 512 MB\", \"Flash memory 256 MB\", \"Fan 2 x fixed fans\", no PoE section at all, 440 x 267.5 x 43.6 mm, 3.35 kg. Management is web/cloud only: the datasheet lists SSH \"No\", HTTP login \"Yes\", HTTPS login \"Yes\", eWeb, SNMPv1/v2c/v3 and Ruijie Cloud / Reyee App; there is no console port and no serial CLI in the datasheet, so no cli capability and no console interface. Layer 2+ software: \"IEEE 802.1Q VLAN Yes\", \"LACP Yes\", \"STP/RSTP/MSTP Yes\", \"DHCP client Yes\", \"DHCP relay Yes\", \"DHCP server No\", \"IPv4 static route Yes\", \"IPv6 static route Yes\" - static routes and relay, no dynamic routing protocol is listed. Port names ge1..geN / sfp1..sfpN / sfp+1..sfp+4 are the catalogue naming convention for a web-managed access switch; the datasheet states port counts, not names. The product page hero block prints \"Forwarding Rate 96 Mpps\" and a \"PoE Budget 370W\" panel that belong to the PoE members of the family; the datasheet figure 95.23 Mpps and the absence of any PoE row are recorded.",
